    "text": "- **High-level functionality**: The function merges overlapping intervals from a list of interval pairs. It sorts the intervals by their start times and then iterates through them to merge any that overlap, updating the end time of the current interval if necessary.\n\n- **Time complexity**: O(n log n) due to the sorting step, where n is the number of intervals. The subsequent iteration over the sorted intervals takes linear time, O(n).\n\n- **Space complexity**: O(n) for storing the result list and the sorted intervals list.\n\n- **Correctness bug**: The function does not handle cases where intervals are identical (e.g., `[1, 3]` and `[1, 3]`). It should merge these as well. This can be fixed by changing the condition `if start < current[1]:` to `if start <= current[1]:`.\n\n- **Performance improvement**: The function could be optimized by using a more efficient sorting algorithm or by implementing a custom sort if the intervals have specific properties (e.g., all intervals are already partially sorted). Additionally, converting tuples to lists and back can be avoided by directly working with tuples.",
